{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913674-playing-as-vampire-in-a-mixed-party","id":913674,"title":"Playing as Vampire in a Mixed Party","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-13T14:59:35-07:00","id":913674,"title":"Playing as Vampire in a Mixed Party","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> The campaign is Hunter the Vigil-based, but we decided to let the player plays as template, if he wishes. So, one player is a Werewolf, another one is a Human from Malleus Maleficarion, other is a Purified (Immortal Handbook) and the last one is a Breed (from Changing Breeds).<br /> My question is, during the character creation, some show interest to play as vampire. But, i guess vampire in the middle of this templates is a little complicated. and I'm not talking about roleplaying or another dramatic question, but just mechanical. The reason is simple: the vampire can only plays during the night. It means that the player can take the risk to remains inactive during the game session and this is boring.<br /> Different if a entire party is vampire, so the characters and Storyteller can focus in the night campaign and everyone can act together.<br /> My question is: did you already experience to play with a vampire template between mixed players? How do you deal with the situation that i mentioned above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:03:39-07:00","id":913708,"title":"","content":"Depending on what edition you're using, vampires now have a <i>slightly </i>easier time operating during the day in 2nd Ed. If a character's Blood Potency is low enough, and her Humanity high enough, going out during the day is merely unpleasant, rather than utterly deadly (the sun does lethal damage to start, not aggravated). It's like being slowly baked to death. It's costly, though, as she'll likely have to spend blood to heal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T18:08:12-07:00","id":913771,"title":"","content":"^This. In 2e, a low Blood Potency, high Humanity character can be out and about during the day for at least short trips. It's <i>painful,</i> since they're taking a bit of lethal damage a few times an hour, but it's not &quot;death in seconds&quot; anymore. Sunlight-induced instantaneous disintegration is now more a thing for vampires with thicker blood and a looser grasp on what it's like to be human.<br /> <br /> The character could also bundle up to reduce their effective Blood Potency for the purposes of calculating how often they take damage, which - at Storyteller discretion, at least - could allow a BP 1 vampire to totally avoid sunlight damage so long as only their eyes are exposed. Sure they'll still get weird looks unless it's frigid out, but better that than sunburns.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the daysleep issue, but it's not impossible to work around that either. An Ordo member (if the player has any status with them) with just a bit of investment in the Ascendant coil can spend a little extra Vitae periodically in order to circumvent the issue entirely <i>and</i> get full Blush of Life perks, for example. Plus there's that one Scale that inverts their sleeping pattern...<br /> <br /> So yeah, sunlight's still Bad, but the Kindred aren't helpless against it anymore as of 2e. If it's 1e though... good luck to them? Maybe houseruling to borrow from 2e a little, or something similar, would be an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:53:06-07:00","id":927101,"title":"","content":"During the day they would probably have to play in the tunnels or find a way to stop the sun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}